      "writtenOn": "2021-11-17T07:12:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this works, but it was really difficult to figure out the interactions between this and mMatchSubscriberIds. Do you want to describe here what should happen to saving/restoring the subscriber ID, including how mMatchSubscriberIds here ?\nIt could be something like :\n\n  The rule describes how the plan should behave, and after restore it should\n  still have the same limits/\u003cwhatever\u003e. The subscriber ID however is local to\n  this device and it would not make sense to save it and restore it (it may\n  point to a subscription that doesn\u0027t exist on the new device, and the new\n  device may not even have the same carrier anyway).\n  mMatchSubscriberIds is computed by NPMS and represents a list of subscriber\n  IDs to check for for a particular carrier. This list also depends on the\n  device and will be recomputed for a given subscriber ID.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 856,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 856,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "6816be13b7bebbec1a9d7abeb5f626f0333c5842",
