      "writtenOn": "2021-11-19T06:28:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmmm not sure what confuses you, but above description is not exactly correct:\n1. subscriber Id is a global unique id that represent the sim card, so we did backup it at l.853.\n2. mMatchSubscriberIds is not necessarily need to be computed by NPMS. Anyone needs to match networks with multiple IMSI at the same time can set mMatchSubscriberIds.\n3. Their interaction is inside the matchesSubscriberId. Where it checks rule \u003d\u003d MATCH_RULL_ALL(don\u0027t care about the NetworkIdentity IMSI) || (template IMSIs contains NetworkIdentity IMSI)\n````\npublic boolean matchesSubscriberId(@Nullable String subscriberId) {\n        return mSubscriberIdMatchRule \u003d\u003d SUBSCRIBER_ID_MATCH_RULE_ALL\n                || ArrayUtils.contains(mMatchSubscriberIds, subscriberId);\n    }\n````                \n\nSo I\u0027ll say to put the below javadoc at the definition of mSubscriberIdMatchRule. See if it solve your concern:\nThe subscriber Id match rule defines how the template should match networks with specific subscriberId(s). See NetworkTemplate#SUBSCRIBER_ID_MATCH_RULE_* for detail.",
      "parentUuid": "74031ec9_74f10609",
      "range": {
